WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:06.990
The world of Pokemon is a bright, colorful
place full of unusual animals.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.550
And if you're anything like the average gamer,
you've spent hundreds of hours wandering through

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.090
the wilderness, looking for Pocket Monsters
to fight, kidnap, and train to battle for

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.090
you.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.579
It's a vicious cycle, and that underlying
weirdness has given rise to some of the strangest,

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:24.249
creepiest video game bootlegs and mods of
any series out there.

00:00:24.249 --> 00:00:28.660
After seeing these Pokemon bootlegs, we're
not sure if you'll want to catch 'em all.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.970
Pokemon “Creepy” Black

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:34.910
The bizarre rumor of Pokemon “Creepy”
Black first popped up around 2005 when someone

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.550
supposedly found an all-black Game Boy cart
at a flea market.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.210
The game gives you the option to start out
with your standard Pokemon, but you can also

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:48.580
start out with Ghost, a Pokemon that can do
only one thing: instantly terrify other Pokemon

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.940
and trainers to death.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:54.010
By the end of the game, your trusty Ghost
turns on you, and you too are dragged into

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:55.830
the cold, cold ground.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:00.350
As with most online horror stories, Pokemon
“Creepy” Black probably wasn't a legit

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:04.530
cart, but the weird Internet story inspired
multiple modders to bring the game to life

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.720
in ROM form.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:10.000
Download it if you'd like a sleepless night
or two, pondering the ethics of being a Pokemon

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.000
trainer.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.050
Just watch out for those Ghost-types.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.800
The creepy doesn’t stop there, however...

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:15.800
Hypno's Lullaby

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:21.050
A mod that arose from a creepypasta poem,
Hypno's Lullaby is all about the strange,

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:25.360
hypnotic Pokemon and his secret penchant for
kidnapping small children and bringing them

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.400
to his cave in Berry Forest.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.100
One could argue that every single Pokemon
deserves a bit of revenge for how they're

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:36.270
treated by their trainers, and Hypno's Lullaby
exacts that revenge tenfold.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.730
Your hero really has no option but to grab
a starter Pokemon and wander into the woods,

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:44.860
where you're immediately captured by Hypno
and trapped in a cave with other zonked-out

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:45.860
kids.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.740
As you work your way out of the cave, you
can only order your Pokemon to kill Hypno's

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.210
juvenile slaves, who block every exit.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.729
Then, you work your way through a tower full
of unbeatable ghosts and the spirits of children

00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:57.810
you've killed.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:01.740
Eventually, Hypno throws one last barrage
of children at you before trapping you in

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.380
a room where he eats your dreams for all eternity.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.690
There is no end; you just shut off the game
and quietly walk away, telling no one what

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:09.690
you’ve done.

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:14.069
There’s even more for you, however, if you
like your Pokemon full of death and despair.

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:15.640
Pokemon Snakewood

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:21.099
Pokemon Ruby is a popular Pokemon game to
mod, and Pokemon Snakewood is just one strange

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.830
example of the results.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.820
Snakewood crosses Pokemon with The Walking
Dead.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:30.670
The result is a game in a post-apocalyptic
setting populated by zombies and demons, where

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:35.160
even the Pokemon have adorably creepy names
like Poliwraith and Headoom.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:40.020
In true Walking Dead style, your hero wakes
up in a destroyed town, encounters someone

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.750
being attacked by zombies, and finds a safe
zone.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.000
As you play, you eventually battle the Four
Horsemen of the Apocalypse, which is a lot

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.580
scarier than just battling some spoiled kid
who likes forcing animals to fight one another.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.660
It's a surprisingly robust story for an unofficial
game.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:58.740
Snakewood proves that Pokemon has its fair
share of inventive—and weird—fans.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.950
Pokemon Quartz

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:06.290
Do you love the concept of Pokemon but hate
all of those corporate, Nintendo-approved

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.290
monsters?

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.599
Well, Pokemon Quartz may be the game for you.

00:03:09.599 --> 00:03:14.810
Dedicated Pokemon bootleggers made a copy
of Ruby and replaced all of the official Pokemon

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.440
sprites with their own malformed creations.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.020
While these Pocket Monsters' names and appearances
have changed, their powers and stats remain

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.020
intact.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.160
Why have the Charmanders been replaced with
these?

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.750
Our best scientists are still working on an
answer.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.920
Quartz is criticized for being relatively
amateurish and incomplete, but the visual

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:37.599
overhaul of so many lovable and popular Pokemon
is just so weirdly obsessive… and pointless...

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:39.870
that it can't be ignored.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:40.870
Pokemon Sweet

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:46.280
Modded from FireRed, Pokemon Sweet reimagines
the entire world of Pokemon as a surreal,

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.800
Candy Kingdom-like place.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:52.660
Here, everything is made of desserts, and
delicious danger lurks around every corner.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:57.280
Because just walking around cotton candy fields
isn't enough, your favorite Pokemon, now called

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.640
Pokesweets, are now named after snacks.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:03.930
Bulbasaur becomes Brownisaur and gets a dollop
of whipped cream and a cherry.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.510
And Popsichu... has a giant wooden stick shoved
into its head.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:12.030
Pokemon types are now flavors instead, and
you basically just ruined your dinner.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.130
The deadliest attack in the game?

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:15.130
Diabetes.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.530
Moemon Emerald / FireRed

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:21.990
For those who want their Pokemon experience
to be even weirder, Moemon is for you.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:26.940
Moemon replaces all of those totally unattractive
monsters with sprites of cosplay girls dressed

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:32.160
up as Pokemon instead, raising even more ethical
questions than the original.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.210
Because pitting animals in deathmatches against
one another isn't horrifying enough, you now

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:41.380
send costumed girls into the arena to fight
one another until one finally passes out from

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.410
the pain.

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:46.940
Instead of building your Pokemon collection,
you slowly grow a violent, confusing little

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:47.940
harem.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.400
Pokemon AshGray

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:54.020
True Pokenerds know the differences between
the original Pokemon games and the anime of

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.300
the same name.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:59.770
AshGray inventively tweaks the original game's
script and missions to actually follow the

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:05.020
events of the offshoot media, including many
episode-specific events, from giving donuts

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:09.190
to Primeapes to leaving Pikachu to live with
other Pikachu in the forest.

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:13.940
The result is a carton of Easter eggs for
devotees of the Pokemon universe, who may

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:18.020
have found the original games lacking after
seeing the more colorful anime.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.970
If the cartoon isn’t your thing, however,
there are even more options for players who

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:25.930
want something more out of Pokemon than just
grinding for Gengars.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.460
Pokemon Advanced Adventure

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:33.449
As far as narrative structure goes, the Pokemon
anime series is still pretty flimsy.

00:05:33.449 --> 00:05:37.610
Ash doesn't have any real motivation to be
the best Pokemon trainer in the world, aside

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:41.750
from the fact that it's something to do in
a world without standardized education or

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.550
non-Pokemon-based employment opportunities.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:49.919
Pokemon Advanced Adventure flips the script
and rewrites Ash as a kid struggling against

00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:55.350
poverty, genetically modified Pokemon, and
Professor Oak's insane, tyrannical grandson

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:58.300
whose only purpose is to train Pokemon to
kill.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:02.950
Finally, Ash is written as an actual hero,
and not just some animal hoarder with dozens

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:04.480
of neglected pets.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.610
Pokemon Vietnamese Crystal

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:10.830
While most of these games are intentionally
strange, there are also a few examples that

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:14.200
are amazing by accident, like Pokemon Vietnamese
Crystal.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:19.360
Fake Pokemon carts are a huge business, and
Kotaku reports that this was a genuine bootleg

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:23.509
that circulated in Vietnam before it was poorly
translated into English.

00:06:23.509 --> 00:06:28.550
As a result, the game's text is hilarious:
it regularly drops profanity, calls Pokemon

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.570
"elves," and barely attempts to make sense.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:35.380
Since it's just a mistranslated Pokemon game
without any big changes, it plays just fine,

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:38.800
if you can make the right text selections
through the garbled menus and figure out what

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:43.479
the game means by phrases like "volcano bakemeat"...
which kinda sounds exactly like something

00:06:43.479 --> 00:06:45.340
Guy Fieri would serve.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.550
2003 Pocket Monster Carbuncle

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:53.199
Unlike most Pokemon bootlegs, which just tweak
existing code, 2003 Pocket Monster Carbuncle

00:06:53.199 --> 00:06:57.289
actually attempts some originality, according
to a GeekParty review.

00:06:57.289 --> 00:07:02.690
The resulting game plays a bit like the classic
NES Dragon Warrior, but also reduces the number

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:05.960
of Pokemon to 20, tossing biodiversity out
the window.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:10.360
The word "carbuncle" usually refers to a cluster
of boils, which would be appropriate enough

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:15.510
for this game, but it's also an obscure word
for a red gemstone, which fits in with Pokemon's

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:18.550
recurring theme of naming games after fancy
rocks.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:23.070
Unfortunately, 2003 Pocket Monster Carbuncle
is a garbage game, and it doesn't play like

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:27.949
Pokemon in any sense whatsoever, but points
for trying something new, unknown foreign

00:07:27.949 --> 00:07:29.039
plagiarizers!

00:07:29.039 --> 00:07:30.280
Pocket Monsters GO!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.280
GO!

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.280
GO!

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:34.319
Now, we enter the realm of the truly terrible.

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:39.259
For no reason whatsoever, other than to dupe
unsuspecting Pokemon fans, some horrible soul

00:07:39.259 --> 00:07:44.530
switched out sprites from The Smurfs' Nightmare
for Game Boy Color, made it run at half speed,

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.740
and pretended it was a Pokemon game.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:51.180
Even the most lonely fanfic writers never
asked for a Smurfs/Pokemon crossover, but

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.660
anything is possible when you have no friends.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:57.730
Starting off your adventure, you’re greeted
by a talking Meowth head who rambles the following:

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:00.860
"Every night in my dreams I see you, I feel
you.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:02.699
You are here so I very fear.

00:08:02.699 --> 00:08:04.590
There is some hate that will not go away."

00:08:04.590 --> 00:08:09.490
Then, you send your morbidly obese Pikachu
through some kind of Satan Town with flickering,

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:10.830
seizure-inducing backgrounds.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:14.870
You then quickly pull the cart out of your
Game Boy and throw it across the room before

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.090
it's too late.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:18.810
Pokemon Stadium: Super Nintendo Edition

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:23.710
Despite Pokemon's relentless popularity, there
was never an official game made for the original

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:26.360
Nintendo Entertainment System or the Super
Nintendo.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:31.880
In fact, the first major Pokemon game for
consoles was the Nintendo 64's Pokemon Stadium,

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:37.649
so it makes little sense to reverse engineer
an N64 cartridge to an older gaming system.

00:08:37.649 --> 00:08:42.929
The SNES was pretty outdated by this time,
so making bootlegs of imaginary games wasn’t

00:08:42.929 --> 00:08:44.569
really economically viable.

00:08:44.569 --> 00:08:49.600
It's like trying to sell a fake dial-up modem;
even if it’s real, no one needs one anymore.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:54.560
Much like the real Pokemon Stadium, the SNES
bootleg is a turn-based fighter, but with

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.639
a limited roster of twelve Pokemon.

00:08:56.639 --> 00:09:02.889
They all have incorrect names: Diglett is
Dagut, Mewtwo is Mu, and Jigglypuff is Pulin.

00:09:02.889 --> 00:09:07.600
It's a fully functional game, unlike most
bootlegs, but it's a step in the wrong direction,

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.009
just like the final game in our list...

00:09:09.009 --> 00:09:11.399
Pokemon 4-in-1

00:09:11.399 --> 00:09:16.319
Another relic from the age of the original
Nintendo, Pokémon 4-in-1 is one of those

00:09:16.319 --> 00:09:22.350
terrible anthology games that crams four games
onto a cart to apologize for all of them sucking.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:26.079
And again, because the Nintendo Entertainment
System was becoming a thing of the past by

00:09:26.079 --> 00:09:29.540
the time Pokémon was popular, this is just
weird.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:33.929
The game includes Picaclick, where you click
on groups of matching symbols; Picadance,

00:09:33.929 --> 00:09:39.250
where you tap on Pokéballs in time to a song;
Picaslot, which is a slot machine for amateur

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.399
gamblers, and…

00:09:41.399 --> 00:09:42.480
Pac-Man.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.230
Which is Pac-Man, but with a disembodied Pikachu
head.

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:50.649
Every single aspect of this is a waste of
money and time, but because it’s bizarre

00:09:50.649 --> 00:09:55.319
and obscure, Pokecollectors will sell their
Pokekidneys to get their hands on one.

00:09:55.319 --> 00:09:56.320
Thanks for watching!

00:09:56.320 --> 00:10:00.220
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:04.570
And leave us a comment to let us know which
bootleg Pokemon game you think is the weirdest...

